  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Railroad workforce recovery: deploying integrated safety shields for infrastructure repair</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ukrzaliznytsia (UZ) is implementing a strategic workforce protection and sector resilience program. By deploying portable signal-monitoring units, the project aims to create a &quot;Safety Shield&quot; that allows reconstruction efforts to proceed in high-risk corridors and locations. This project serves as a pilot for &quot;Resilient Infrastructure&quot; protocols, aligning UZ with the TEN-T safety requirements for high-risk corridors.    

Designed for deployment across priority rail corridors, these devices provide real-time monitoring of the radio frequency spectrum to identify potential aerial threats. By providing immediate audible and visual alerts, this equipment ensures the operational continuity of locomotive crews, recovery trains, and essential personnel at critical infrastructure sites during reconstruction and maintenance activities. It is a foundational step in modernizing labor standards and ensuring the continuity of the national logistics backbone during a period of intensive rebuilding.

The data collected by these &quot;shields&quot; will be integrated into the Situational Center, transforming UZ into a data-driven infrastructure manager.</narrative>
  </description>
